\textbf{Retained alternatives can remain useful when requirements change.}
At four verified draws, Re:Dr and Re:Max improve \texttt{Graph} portfolio survival after a binding option withdrawal by $19.65$ and $10.99$ percentage points over their matched controls (App.~\ref{app:portfolio-withdrawals}). In a two-seed recovery study, Re:Dr reduces recovery calls under ordinary and temperature-tuned sampling across all five domains, while diversity prompting reverses the \texttt{Pantry} advantage (App.~\ref{app:withdrawal-recovery}).

